---
/**
 * /disclaimer/ .
 *
 * IT EXISTS BECAUSE THIS IS YMYL CONTENT, NOT BECAUSE A TEMPLATE HAD A SLOT FOR
 * IT. Google holds financial content to a higher standard than most, crypto is
 * the part of financial content it holds to the highest standard of all, and the
 * author's professional reputation is the entire reason any of these sites
 * exists. A publication about money that never states its own limits is making a
 * claim by omission.
 *
 * IT IS ALSO THE PAGE THAT PROVES THE NEGATION LOGIC IN
 * scripts/verify-subject.mjs WORKS. This page necessarily contains the phrases
 * "investment advice" and the names of professional designations, because saying
 * that none of them applies is its whole job. A gate that could not tell "is
 * investment advice" from "is not investment advice" would force this page to be
 * deleted in order to pass, which inverts the rule it enforces. So the gate reads
 * the sentence around each match and skips a negated one, and this page is the
 * live test of that.
 *
 * WHAT IT MUST NEVER BECOME. It is not a disambiguation page. Nothing here
 * distinguishes the author from anybody, and no sentence on this site does.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Datum from "../components/Datum.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { routeMeta } from "../lib/seo";

const trail = [{ label: "Disclaimer", href: "/disclaimer/" }];
---

<Base {...routeMeta.disclaimer} breadcrumbs={trail}>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={trail} />

  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <span class="eyebrow__num">00</span>
        <span>Limits, stated plainly</span>
      </p>
      <h1 style="max-width: 20ch;">What this site is not.</h1>
      <p class="page-head__lede">
        ISM50 publishes history. Everything below is a limit on what that means,
        written once so no article has to carry a paragraph of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <Datum label="Not advice" />

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Nothing here is investment advice</h2>
        <p>
          No article on this site is investment advice, financial advice or
          trading advice, and none of it is a recommendation to buy, to sell or to
          hold anything. Nothing here is guidance for a reader's own
          circumstances. The site quotes no price target, states no view on what
          any asset is worth, and makes no forecast about what anything will do
          next.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is not a lawyer's sentence bolted onto an opinion site. It is a
          description of what the writing actually does. Every piece is about a
          period that has already finished, written with hindsight the people
          involved did not have, and the recurring finding is that the people
          closest to an event usually could not read it correctly at the time.
          Anyone who took that seriously would be slower to make a prediction, not
          quicker.
        </p>

        <h2>No professional designation is claimed</h2>
        <p>
          The author is not a Chartered Professional Accountant, is not a
          Chartered Accountant, is not a Certified Public Accountant and is not a
          Chartered Financial Analyst. He holds no accounting designation and no
          analyst designation of any kind, and nothing on this site should be read
          as claiming one. He is a consultant, which is the accurate word.
        </p>
        <p>
          He is also not acting as anybody's adviser, agent or fiduciary by
          publishing this, and reading it creates no professional relationship of
          any sort.
        </p>

        <h2>The history is checked, and it is still history</h2>
        <p>
          Every factual claim on this site is meant to be traceable to a source a
          reader can open, and where a claim is contested the contest is named
          rather than resolved. That is a standard, not a guarantee. Primary
          sources in this subject disappear, get edited, and are sometimes wrong
          in the first place, and a piece written carefully today can be
          superseded by a document that surfaces later.
        </p>
        <p>
          If something here is wrong, the correction is worth more than the
          original. It gets made on the page, with the change noted, rather than
          quietly.
        </p>

        <h2>No tax guidance appears here, deliberately</h2>
        <p>
          This site does not write about what anybody owes anyone. That subject
          belongs to
          <a href="https://khaledhawari.ca/about-khaled-hawari/">khaledhawari.ca</a>,
          which is the author's practice and covers it properly. The separation is
          enforced by the build rather than by memory: a verifier fails the build
          if the vocabulary appears on this domain at all.
        </p>

        <h2>Links out</h2>
        <p>
          Sources are linked because a reader should be able to check them.
          Linking a document is not an endorsement of whoever published it, and
          this site has no control over what a third party does with a URL after
          it is cited. Where a link has died, the piece says so and says what the
          document said.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
